WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.290
Hunter x Hunter has returned with a series
of brand new manga chapters after being on

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:13.620
hiatus for 1423 days. That’s almost 4 years
without a chapter. After many fans had already

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.789
given up on ever seeing the continuation of
this fantastic and unique story, Hisoka and

00:00:18.789 --> 00:00:23.890
co finally have their big come back. However
you might not be aware of the bitter sweet

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:30.320
story behind the long hiatus, how close Hunter
x Hunter actually was to being done for good

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:36.300
and how in the end Yoshihiro Togashi overcame
the massive odds stacked against him and his

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:42.190
work to actually make it to publication once
more. It’s a story of pain, sickness, the

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:47.840
curse of being a genius writer and of a man
who has dedicated his everything to his work

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.090
and his fans. And while it’s already clear
that this new material is seamlessly picking

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:57.809
up with the high quality it left off on, after
such a long time, it’s easy to lose track

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:02.510
of what is going on right now in the story,
what characters are important and what you

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:08.430
can expect of the upcoming chapters and the
overall future of the story. This is everything

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:12.140
you need to know about the long awaited return
of Hunter x Hunter.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:16.880
There aren’t too many stories that can allow
themselves to suddenly go on an unannounced

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:23.390
and open-ended hiatus and then come back four
years later to an euphoric fanbase that is

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:28.850
more excited and hungry for new stories than
ever before. That alone should give you a

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:35.170
taste of how special Hunter x Hunter truly
is as a story. After years of complete silence

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:40.671
since it’s last chapter in weekly shounen
jump magazine on November 26th 2018, with

00:01:40.671 --> 00:01:46.670
none knowing what the status of the story
was and why there had been no news for so

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:52.619
long, author Yoshihiro Togashi appeared out
of nowhere on a brand new Twitter profile

00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:58.590
on May 24th 2022, with the following tweet:
とりあえずあと４話 - 4 more chapters

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:03.130
left for now. Togashi must have expected all
kinds of reactions to this tweet: Maybe no

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:08.509
one would notice it, maybe people would be
angry with him for practically ghosting his

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:14.239
fanbase for 4 years, or even worse: Maybe
people had stopped caring for his story all

00:02:14.239 --> 00:02:16.600
together and moved on.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:23.200
What happened next is something that neither
he nor anyone else could have ever imagined:

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:29.860
The entire internet exploded. And I really
mean that: I have never seen anything like

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:36.500
it happen before. The most unlikely assortment
of people you could imagine came together

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:41.950
to celebrate the corner of a manga page with
a sketch that looked like someone had played

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:46.640
around with his pen and forgotten to put the
cap on it. From massive YouTubers like Mr

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:54.680
Beast to the most random brands like KFC or
Axe, everyone was excited about the prospect

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:59.860
of this man’s scribbles. Togashi’s twitter
account blasted itself to 2 million followers

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:05.900
in a few days and stands at 3 million only
a few months after its launch, where he has

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.630
been publishing updates on his progress.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:14.260
It must have been a true relieve and even
overwhelming to him to see all these positive

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:20.040
responses. But what to an outsider must have
looked like millions of people going absolutely

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:26.050
nuts about a few doodles badly lit paper,
has a very easy explanation. Hunter x Hunter

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:32.129
is a one of a kind story even in the world
of shounen, that at the peak consists of nothing

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:39.360
but high quality stories. Togashi took a look
at main stream shounen manga and decided to

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:45.610
flip its concept on its head, pioneering a
whole sub genre of successful series like

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:51.129
Attack on Titan, Jujutsu Kaisen or Chainsaw
man. He looked at the established format of

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:56.280
major stories like Dragonball, One PIece and
Naruto and wondered what would happen if he

00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:01.180
treated these stories realistically. The result
is that Hunter x Hunter starts out with as

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:07.450
a normal shounen, but its main character gon
goes from cheerfully powerful good boy to

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:12.879
one of the darkest and most disillusioned
characters in modern fiction. The story very

00:04:12.879 --> 00:04:18.169
quickly becomes very dark and very morally
complex. It turns out that a 13 year old who

00:04:18.169 --> 00:04:23.639
thinks there are only good and bad people
will have a hard time in the real world, filled

00:04:23.639 --> 00:04:28.510
with morally ambiguous characters. The story
and its world feel incredibly real and refreshing,

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:33.770
as the intricate politics and challenges of
the world shape its heroes and not the other

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:39.330
way around. Togashi’s character writing
is some of the best, if not the best in all

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:44.770
of manga, each character with incredible depth
and moral complexity. Garnish this with a

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:50.860
fantastic power system like Nen, and you have
a story that is beloved by millions of people.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:56.350
And yet, we almost never got this continuation
of Hunter x Hunter in the first place.

00:04:56.350 --> 00:05:04.229
Yoshihiro Togashi began on March 16 1998 and
has produced 36 volumes with 390 chapters

00:05:04.229 --> 00:05:09.111
in it. Which sounds like a lot, until you
compare it with a story like One PIece, that

00:05:09.111 --> 00:05:16.380
released just one year earlier and has published
over 1000 chapters until today almost 3 times

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:20.919
as many. The reason for this has been the
increasing amount of weeks that Togashi took

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:24.361
off from publishing the story. When you look
at the hunter x hunter hiatus chart, which

00:05:24.361 --> 00:05:29.850
yes, is a real thing, then you can see how
the manga starts out with a lot of blue weeks,

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:36.160
where the manga was published continually
growing redder and redder until around 2006

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:41.229
it switches into long streaks of red and blue
alternating, where the story would go on a

00:05:41.229 --> 00:05:45.949
break for a while and then publish about 10
chapters in a row. These stretches of red

00:05:45.949 --> 00:05:51.419
to produce a handful of chapters get longer
and longer until in 2018 we finally hit that

00:05:51.419 --> 00:05:57.539
big red wall that is the 4 year hiatus we
are just coming out of. What in the world

00:05:57.539 --> 00:06:02.340
is going on here? It turns out that Yoshihiro
Togashi, despite being incredibly passionate

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:07.449
and caring about his work as a mangaka has
been fighting with terrible health problems

00:06:07.449 --> 00:06:12.180
ever since starting the story, that have made
it almost impossible for him to continue his

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:17.010
work. These problems included increasingly
excruciating back and chest pain, that made

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:22.819
it very hard for him to move and draw. On
top of that he started to sleep poorly, which

00:06:22.819 --> 00:06:28.669
soon turned into full blown insomnia, in parts
due to this chronic pain, that kept his body

00:06:28.669 --> 00:06:34.650
from getting the necessary rest it needed
to heal. As a result he became bedridden and

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:40.699
pretty much incapable of working on his story
for weeks and months on end. Togashi eventually

00:06:40.699 --> 00:06:45.729
decided to share this terrible and exhausting
cycle with his fans in a series of author

00:06:45.729 --> 00:06:51.061
notes appearing along the few chapters that
he still managed to release. We don’t know

00:06:51.061 --> 00:06:55.389
for sure, but it’s very likely that his
4 year absence also was caused by his declining

00:06:55.389 --> 00:07:00.319
health as he tried to focus on recovery. Some
people speculated during that time, that maybe

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:08.020
it wasn’t his health after all. Maybe Togashi
had simply written himself into a corner.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:12.220
After writing a pretty much perfect ending
to the adventures of Gon and Killua, he shifted

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:18.419
his focus to setting up the dark continent,
a place that has been hyped up with such high

00:07:18.419 --> 00:07:25.259
expectations, that it would be impossible
to deliver on. And while I’m sure that this

00:07:25.259 --> 00:07:30.740
was part of his struggle during that time,
Togashi has proven often enough how capable

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:35.949
of a writer he truly is, that wouldn’t shy
away from that challenge.

00:07:35.949 --> 00:07:39.879
And indeed, with his return to the public
world through twitter and sharing his progress

00:07:39.879 --> 00:07:44.800
on the recent chapters, fans very optimistic,
not only that they would finally get to see

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:51.009
the dark continent, but also that his condition
must have been improving, some going so far

00:07:51.009 --> 00:07:56.760
as speculating that a continuous weekly release
would be possible again from now on. This

00:07:56.760 --> 00:08:02.790
couldn’t have been further from the truth.
July Togashi admitted was unable to sit upright

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:07.949
and that he was now drawing the line-art for
his remaining chapters while lying down. Until

00:08:07.949 --> 00:08:12.900
august, his health seemed once again to dwindle,
tweeting that he only had finished a single

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:18.569
panel, not having enough strength to keep
the grip on his pen. In this moment, the entire

00:08:18.569 --> 00:08:24.289
project seemed to be at risk of ending right
then and there. However in that moment something

00:08:24.289 --> 00:08:29.009
changed. Whether it was his own will to keep
writing his story and keep his promise to

00:08:29.009 --> 00:08:35.650
his audience or his overall health slowly
improving slightly or a mix of both, Togashi

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:40.760
decided to not give up and keep fighting.
He worked hard and was determined to finish

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:47.300
the 10 chapters for release, which has now
finally happened. And which he must be very

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:53.050
proud of. So with that out of the way, what
exactly is going on right now in the manga?

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:54.810
And where are we going from here?

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:59.450
If you only watched the anime or simply need
a refresher, here is a quick overview what

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:04.870
happened between the chairmain selection arc
and the new chapters: With Gon having no more

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:09.260
Nen and Killua on a wholesome journey with
his little sister, the focus of the story

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:15.950
has now shifted to Kurapika, who is the main
character now as well as Leorio. Both of them

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:21.321
have joined the Zodiacs, the top 12 hunters,
which has started the 9th arc of Hunter x

00:09:21.321 --> 00:09:28.190
Hunter known as the succession war arc. Right
now everything takes place on a giant boat

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:34.430
shaped like a whale, that is traveling towards
the dark continent, which is mostly undiscovered

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:39.810
and filled with powerful nen creatures, such
as the chimera ant queen. On this ship is

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:46.110
a battle royal happening between the 14 Princes
of the Kakin kingdom for who gets to be king,

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:50.440
each having a nen beast at their disposal
for the fight, though the rules really get

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:55.180
quite complicated. The Zodiacs of the hunter
association are on board to escort Isssac

00:09:55.180 --> 00:10:00.300
Netero’s son on his expedition to the dark
continent. Kurapika is there to retrieve the

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:05.560
last of his clan’s missing scarlet eyes
from the fourth prince and main antagonist

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:10.880
Tserriednich. The phantom troop is also there,
looking for Hisoka, who after a death match

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:16.580
with Chrollo that he had wanted for so long,
had killed two of the troops members. As well

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:22.350
as the struggle amongst a number of Mafia
families. All on that boat. So you tell me

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:23.959
if that sounds interesting or not.

00:10:23.959 --> 00:10:28.769
it seems for now that we will be getting a
minimum of 10 chapters and then we can only

00:10:28.769 --> 00:10:33.640
hope that Togashi’s health stabilizes, so
we will see a continuation of the story after

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:38.070
that, hopefully with less than 4 years of
waiting. The new material will continue this

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:42.100
fantastic journey towards the black continent
and will give us the return of some of our

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:48.370
most beloved characters, like Chrollo, Hisoka
and Kurapika, while also introducing a ton

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:54.360
of new fascinating ones. If you want to know
what makes hisoka such a fantastic character

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:57.770
for example, you can watch my analysis of
him next.

